    "title": "Where is March Madness Final Four? Location, dates, schedule",
    "text": "March 28, 2026, 6:04 a.m. ETThe Road to the Final Four and Indianapolis is nearly complete.68 teams set out on Selection Sunday with the goal of winning a national championship at Lucas Oil Stadium in Indianapolis. Since then, and with the near-completion of two full weekends of March Madness games, the Men's NCAA Tournament has delivered some magical moments and upsets, despite also having a lot of chalk.The Final Four matchups will be set by the end of Sunday night, with four teams booking their flights and travel from their respective Elite Eight sites (and campuses) to Indianapolis.The Elite Eight gets underway at 6:09 p.m. ET on Saturday, March 28 with a Big Ten showdown between No. 3 Illinois and No. 9 Iowa. The Big Ten is guaranteed to have at least one team in the Final Four and could have as many as three.Here's what to know on the Final Four for the Men's NCAA Tournament:Where is the Final Four for men's NCAA Tournament?Men's Final Four Location: Lucas Oil Stadium (Indianapolis)The Final Four returns to Lucas Oil Stadium and Indianapolis in 2026 for the Men's NCAA Tournament. It is the first time the Final Four has returned to Indianapolis since the COVID-19 bubble-style tournament in 2021, and the fourth time Lucas Oil Stadium has hosted the Final Four.It will also mark the ninth time that the city of Indianapolis has hosted the Final Four, with the first coming in 1980 at Market Square Arena. It took place inside the RCA Dome four different times.The Final Four is set to return to Lucas Oil Stadium in 2029.When is the Final Four for men's March Madness?Men's Final Four Dates: Saturday, April 4 and Monday, April 6The Final Four of the Men's NCAA Tournament will take place across Saturday, April 4 and Monday, April 6. The national semifinal games will take place on April 4 with tip-off times of 6 p.m. ET and 8:30 p.m. ET, while the national championship will tip off at 8:30 on April 6.Final Four schedule 2026Here's a breakdown of the Final Four schedule for the 2026 NCAA Tournament, including tip-off times and TV channel information:Final FourDate: Saturday, April 4Time: Game 1: 6 p.m. ET | Game 2: 8:30 p.m. ETTV channel: TBSStreaming options: March Madness Live app and SlingTVMarch Madness National ChampionshipDate: Monday, April 6Time: 8:30 p.m. ETTV channel: TBSStreaming options: March Madness Live app and SlingTVThe USA TODAY app gets you to the heart of the news — fast. Download for award-winning coverage, crosswords, audio storytelling, the eNewspaper and more.",
